{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533898-v20-path-of-the-focused-mind","id":1533898,"title":"[V20] Path of the Focused Mind","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-09T13:01:33-07:00","id":1533898,"title":"[V20] Path of the Focused Mind","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I am not sure of how the rules for Path of the Focused Mind work.<br /> <br /> <br /> FIRST QUESTION:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rites of the Blood p. 139</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unlike most Thaumaturgy, <b>the<br /> powers of this Path do not require an action to invoke</b>,<br /> although they still require the normal blood expenditure<br /> and Willpower activation roll. Thaumaturges with this<br /> Path may use any single power from this Path during a<br /> single turn.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Readiness<br /> ...<br /> System: This power is only usable on the thaumaturge<br /> herself.<b> Every success on the activation roll adds one die<br /> to a special dice pool for the remainder of the turn.</b> These<br /> dice may be used on any Wits-related rolls or actions that<br /> the thaumaturge performs during this turn. <b>Alternatively,<br /> each die removed from the dice pool adds one to the<br /> caster\u2019s initiative rating.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>If initiative is rolled before the turn starts, how can the use of the power help you at all? My understanding is: you roll initiative, THEN you can use your Path of Focused Mind 1st dot power on your turn, the special die pool could be used for the initiative BUT it was already rolled... So what good is it for if it only last one turn?<br /> <br /> Can someone clarify?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> SECOND QUESTION:<br /> The 4th dot power describes:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dual Thought, Rites of the Blood P. 140</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">System: <b>Successful use of Dual Thought allows the<br /> caster to take two actions without penalty during her turn</b>.<br /> (Note that this power specifically lifts the restrictions of\u200b<br /> multiple actions detailed in V20, p. 248.)<b> The extra action<br /> granted by this power must be a mental action</b>, whether<br /> it\u2019s the use of Disciplines such as the use of Auspex or<br /> Thaumaturgy, or the contemplation of some problem.<br /> If the character is using both actions to solve a problem,<br /> she has two separate dice pools to draw from. These two<br /> actions happen at the same time, as determined by the<br /> initiative rating of the character. <b>You may not use the<br /> extra action to re-cast Dual Thought.\u200b</b></div> </div> </div> </div>If the powers do not require an action to invoke, and you get a normal and an EXTRA mental action, could you use the <i>normal </i>action to recast Dual Thought? The restriction is on the extra action, not the normal one as I can read.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 04-10-2024, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T21:33:56-07:00","id":1533931,"title":"","content":"Off hand those look like poorly written powers.<br /> <br /> 1) Yeah, I don't think it can work as written. Each turn your roll your Initiative you roll a d10 and add your Dex+Wits. So let's say the character goes 3rd. When their turn comes up, they can't increase their Initiative, or at least it won't do any good because the other two characters have already acted. Further, the pool only lasts for the one turn, so they can't spend points to increase their initiative for the next turn. <br /> <br /> My recommendation is to allow a character to spend points to increase their initiative for the next turn. So if they take 4 points away, then the next time they roll Initiative at the top of the next turn, they'll get an extra 4 points to the roll. Alternatively, you could let a character activate this power outside of the normal action sequence, while Initiative is being rolled, letting them choose to boost their initiative. <br /> <br /> 2) By RAW, no, you can't use your normal action to re-activate the power because you don't use actions to activate the power in the first place. I think it's pretty clear that the author forgot that Focused Mind powers don't require actions to activate. Technically you could activate it an unlimited number of times per turn. So what happens? One ruling is that it would just let you take an unlimited number of actions (until you run out of blood point). That's obviously busted as fuck. Alternatively there could be another reading focusing on the first bolded line the main thing - it allows the caster to take 2 actions without penalty per turn. So if you've already taken two actions this turn, activating it again won't add more actions, the power will just be wasted. I think the easiest solution is to just rule that the power can only be activated once per turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T02:07:50-07:00","id":1533943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533898-v20-path-of-the-focused-mind#post1533898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If initiative is rolled before the turn starts, how can the use of the power help you at all? My understanding is: you roll initiative, THEN you can use your Path of Focused Mind 1st dot power on your turn, the special die pool could be used for the initiative BUT it was already rolled... So what good is it for if it only last one turn?</div> </div> </div> </div>Initiative modifiers like that happen on initiative, so I would allow the player the choice whether they want to spend a BP before they roll and activate the power. Since it's not an action, I don't see a problem there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533898-v20-path-of-the-focused-mind#post1533898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the powers do not require an action to invoke, and you get a normal and an EXTRA mental action, could you use the <i>normal </i>action to recast Dual Thought? The restriction is on the extra action, not the normal one as I can read.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yesn't. Keep in mind there is a limit set by Generation how many BPs a vampire can spend per turn. Up to 10th gen, it's just one. There are ways around that obviously (Blood of Potency), but at worst it becomes a poor man's Celerity for mental feats<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T03:18:21-07:00","id":1533947,"title":"","content":"As for question 1, it is as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> said. Reflexive actions like spending blood are still actions and yet don't happen according to initiative. The powers of the Path are not even actions, they are faster than reflexive actions. <br /> <br /> As for question 2, there is another limit to this path that isn't in what you quoted here @Ibeaumanior, namely that can only use one power of this road, once, per turn. So casting Dual Thought twice is not possible anyway. The authors specified it just in case players and ST forgot that limitation (which is written in the same paragraph that says powers from this path don't require actions to cast).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T04:46:14-07:00","id":1533952,"title":"","content":"They're resolved during the &quot;ask players if anyone is using Celerity&quot; phase of the turn, so the storyteller can plan appropriately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T07:21:13-07:00","id":1533968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533898-v20-path-of-the-focused-mind?p=1533947#post1533947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for question 1, it is as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> said. Reflexive actions like spending blood are still actions and yet don't happen according to initiative. The powers of the Path are not even actions, they are faster than reflexive actions.<br /> <br /> As for question 2, there is another limit to this path that isn't in what you quoted here @Ibeaumanior, namely that can only use one power of this road, once, per turn. So casting Dual Thought twice is not possible anyway. The authors specified it just in case players and ST forgot that limitation (which is written in the same paragraph that says powers from this path don't require actions to cast).</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"16965\" data-vbnamecard=\"16965\">Hermeticus</a><br /> You are right, I forgot to copy that part of the text. Added.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T07:22:00-07:00","id":1533969,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"16965\" data-vbnamecard=\"16965\">Hermeticus</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar431_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"431\" data-vbnamecard=\"431\">Theodrim</a> thanks for your replies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T09:11:09-07:00","id":1533977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533898-v20-path-of-the-focused-mind?p=1533943#post1533943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Initiative modifiers like that happen on initiative, so I would allow the player the choice whether they want to spend a BP before they roll and activate the power. Since it's not an action, I don't see a problem there.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yesn't. Keep in mind there is a limit set by Generation how many BPs a vampire can spend per turn. Up to 10th gen, it's just one. There are ways around that obviously (Blood of Potency), but at worst it becomes a poor man's Celerity for mental feats</div> </div> </div> </div>You make me doubt, how does this combine with Celerity extra actions? Could you explain, I am not really clear on the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T09:44:37-07:00","id":1533979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533898-v20-path-of-the-focused-mind?p=1533977#post1533977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You make me doubt, how does this combine with Celerity extra actions? Could you explain, I am not really clear on the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry if was misleading, I just compared the two on a functional basis. You wouldn't be able to combine the Path with Celerity, because the additional actions gained through Celerity must be physical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T21:27:47-07:00","id":1534011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533898-v20-path-of-the-focused-mind?p=1533947#post1533947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for question 1, it is as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> said. Reflexive actions like spending blood are still actions and yet don't happen according to initiative. The powers of the Path are not even actions, they are faster than reflexive actions.<br /> <br /> As for question 2, there is another limit to this path that isn't in what you quoted here @Ibeaumanior, namely<b> that can only use one power of this road, once, per turn.</b> So casting Dual Thought twice is not possible anyway. The authors specified it just in case players and ST forgot that limitation (which is written in the same paragraph that says powers from this path don't require actions to cast).</div> </div> </div> </div>So, blood per turn not considered, you could use all power of the path, once per turn without care for the initiative order?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T21:57:59-07:00","id":1534014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533898-v20-path-of-the-focused-mind?p=1534011#post1534011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, blood per turn not considered, you could use all power of the path, once per turn without care for the initiative order?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a bit unsure at the moment on how the phrasing of the limitation in the manual should be taken, but my current understanding is that only one power from this Path can be cast per turn, once. Some powers last multiple turns though, so they can be cast and then they will still be active in later turns while other powers from the Path are cast in those turns.<br /> <br /> But yes, it's regardless of \u0130nitiaitve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}